# Manifest of the gd test suites scripts/run-gd-tests.sh MUST find under
# cad/tests/gd/. Line format (v2, shared with pcb/tests/gd/EXPECTED_SUITES):
#
#     <filename> [assertions=N] [real-worker]
#
# - <filename>: exactly as it appears on disk. A suite going missing
#   (deleted, renamed, moved off the glob) or appearing unregistered is a
#   loud, named pre-flight failure in both directions.
# - assertions=N: the suite must report exactly N total assertions
#   (passed+failed). This is what makes `check(true); quit(0)` planted above
#   the real assertions FAIL instead of passing a bare `n_pass > 0` floor.
#   When a suite legitimately grows or shrinks, re-pin here in a deliberate,
#   reviewed own-commit — the same act as registering the suite.
# - real-worker: the suite's Results line must prove real_worker_used=true.
#   No cad suite uses it yet; the runner refuses the attribute until
#   cad/scripts/probe-worker-methods.py exists, because the attribute is a
#   claim about a live worker and an unprobed worker cannot back it.
#
# This file is deliberately NOT named test_*.gd (it must not match the
# runner's own `test_*.gd` glob) and NOT executable GDScript.

# Two controls (a normal middle-drag orbits; a received release stops the
# orbit) plus the repro (a LOST middle-button release must not strand the
# camera in orbit).
test_orbit_camera_stuck.gd assertions=3

