# Measuring a foreign mesh: a CSG plate with two plain through holes, one hole
# 1.9 mm from the outline, one drilled 30 degrees off the plate normal, a blind
# pocket and a convex boss, baked in-test and posed by a non-identity
# transform. Pins the propose half (segmentation, plane and cylinder fits,
# facet count, the inscribed-vs-circumscribed distinction, the axis of the
# tilted hole) and the verify half (colliders, refined centres in both frames,
# the pin that actually fits, through vs blind, a too-large gauge reporting
# contacts, the boss verifying while an oversize and an in-mid-air boss
# candidate do not, a gauge buried in solid material refusing to fit, a
# clearance searched to the part's own extent rather than to a multiple of
# the pin, a gauge in open space reporting the search bound as a FLOOR and not
# as a clearance, a mirrored copy and an inward-wound copy each keeping the
# sense of every feature, a pixel-less probe, and the ray-grid fallback's
# limits). Plus two plate stacks sharing a face: the coincident triangles are
# two crossings, so a pin in open air beyond them still fits. Also that two
# concurrent requests for one file segment it once and both get the answer,
# and that reference scoping holds past Godot's 32 collision layers: a
# blocker sharing the target's final layer is excluded under the target's
# mask, and the SAME job under every layer (name still attached) is shrunk
# by that blocker, so the mask is the scope and the name alone scopes nothing.
test_mesh_measurement.gd assertions=72

