# reference running down the drill cannot change a measurement scoped to
# this one while an UNSCOPED call does see it, that a node= filter is a match
# when any one mounted reference carries it, that a diameter limit is a world
# millimetre under a scaled pose, and that a pose scaled by 2 reports twice
# the diameter in world and the file's own in local. Also that a reference
# set which keeps changing while a verb waits comes back marked stale with a
# reason, and a settled one does not. Also — bug 01a07a19a9e8 — that the
# gauge verb measures the EVALUATED SOLID and not only the references: a
# sphere inside a solid plate mounted through the real interference_world
# path does not fit and reports a WITNESS contact naming the solid (a witness
# is the nearest surface of the body it is inside, not a foul), one standing
# 0.5 mm off it reports that air as a MEASURED clearance (a sphere used to
# report 0 beside the reference box's half diagonal at every position),
# reference= still answers about that reference alone — proved on
# mesh_gauge's own mask guard, with a job carrying the module AND a scope
# where an unscoped one reads solid material — and open space still reports
