# Interference between the evaluated solid and a reference: a CSG board posed
# by a transform that TURNS it as well as moving it, and five solids built
# in-test and handed over as worker mesh data. Pins the solid's collider being
# rebuilt on every evaluation and never cached, a boss driven clean through the
# board reporting the right node with a crossing on the boss circle at a board
# face to 0.05 mm, both frames agreeing under the pose, the penetration coming
# back as the board's own thickness, the same boss lifted 0.1 mm reporting a
# clean zero (with the previous points gone), a 0.2 mm sliver overlap with NO
# vertex of either body inside the other still being reported, a cube buried in
# the board being caught by parity alone, the status line naming the first
# offender, and the reference=/node= scoping (a filter matching nothing
# reports nothing). Plus containment the other way round (a board wholly
# inside the solid, caught by parity alone); the DESIGNED contact — a board
# resting on an open cavity's floor, inside the shell's own bounds, which must
# read as clean and not as containment; and supersession: two overlapping
# requests through a stand-in panel — now THREE, because an evaluation is
# QUEUED and never refused: the one running answers its own document, the one
# displaced in the single queue slot stands down as superseded, the newest
# measures and is the only one whose crossings end up on screen; and a VERB
# refused as busy takes no ticket, so the evaluation it was refused for still
# paints. A ticket belongs to a granted reservation, so the check that was
# running is not overtaken by one that only queued behind it. The displaced
# reply is marked and —
# sampled at the instant it returns, which an end-state assertion could not
# distinguish — never painted, while the pane ends up showing the newest
# answer. And the probe that decides containment: a washer floating inside a
# shell with a locating pin standing through its mounting hole, whose every
# vertex is on a rim of that hole and whose rim is narrower than the module's
# own inset step — so every candidate probe lands in the hole, inside the pin,
# and a probe that is not verified to be inside its OWN body reports the
# washer as buried in the shell; having offered no probe at all, that washer
# comes back UNDECIDED rather than clean. Also the same washer and a locating
# pin as TWO NODES OF ONE REFERENCE inside a solid block: the pin's material must not
# vouch for the washer (no pair may claim it), the washer's containment is
# reported as UNDECIDED with a reason and said so on the banner, and the pin —
# which does offer a probe inside itself — is reported under the record's own
# bare node path. And the reservation: a request arriving while a check is
# INSIDE its window is refused as busy, naming the holder's ticket and age,
# while a holder PAST its deadline is reclaimed — its ticket going inert, so
# its own late release cannot hand the collider away from the check that owns
# it now, and the reclaimer's release frees the module normally.
# A reclaimed holder that wakes up writes NOTHING: its rebuild is refused
# (freeing the collider under the live check would be a freed body, not a wrong
# number), the generation is unmoved, and its job answers without measuring.
# A reclaimed holder's writes are all no-ops, and a wrong ticket cannot free
# the collider even when the holder has AGED past its window: only reserve()
# hands the module over.
# And a stack of 40 thin plates with a 0.1 mm cube parked in one of its gaps,
# mounted TWICE under two names: every ray out of that cube crosses more
# surfaces than the gauge's crossing budget allows, so the parity question
# cannot be answered — which must read as UNDECIDED and not as clean — and
# both references whose bounds hold the cube are left open, not just the
# first one found. And parity is per node down to its BUDGET: a plain cube
# sharing its reference with that stack is still decidable, because the
# unrelated node's crossings neither count for it nor spend its count.
# And a cube buried inside TWO identical blocks mounted under two names: being
# inside one body is not an answer about the other, so both are reported, each
# under its own node, and nothing is left undecided.
# And the crossing a FIXED probe step steps over: a 0.004 mm plate — thinner
# than the module's 0.005 mm probe ceiling, thicker than the 0.002 mm sphere
# its parity probe places — with a 4 mm column driven through it must be
# reported as a crossing, which is only possible when the step is measured
# from the material that is actually there — and so must a tall, narrow
# tetrahedron whose single buried vertex sits inside that plate, on ALL THREE
# of its edges: an edge that only LEAVES material has nothing ahead of the
# crossing, so the run has to be measured on both sides of it.
# And the paint belongs to the NEWEST evaluation from the moment it queues: a
# check that is running when a newer evaluation arrives keeps its ticket,
# finishes measuring and answers, but paints nothing — an interfering
# document's crosses must not stand on screen until the queued clean one
# runs — and the queued check paints the pane when its turn comes.
# And a crossing the reference side cannot READ is still a crossing: a
# narrow solid column through the plates of the layered stack, whose parity
# probes on both sides of every crossing run out of budget, is reported on
# the plate faces with the plate's thickness — the tri-state that keeps an
# unreadable probe from clearing a body holds on the reference side as it
# does on the solid side.
# A check that STARTS with a pose rewritten in place and the colliders not
# yet rebuilt — nothing changing during its wait — rebuilds the colliders
# from the records it holds before casting, stamps the report with the
# gauge's own digest, and finds the crossing where the board now is, framed
# in the new pose. And the parity probe's limit is the gauge sphere's
# DIAMETER (mesh_gauge reads a sphere's size as one): a column through a
# 0.003 mm plate is probed and kept, one through a 0.0015 mm plate cannot be
# probed and is kept by the keep-the-crossing rule — both off the plate's
# face diagonals, so the plate's own edges cannot report the crossing.
# And the shared gauge REBUILT under a check in flight: a check parked at its
# physics step when a newer evaluation re-poses in place, rebuilds the
# colliders and queues comes back superseded — unchecked, unstamped,
# unpainted — and the evaluation that rebuilt them is the one measured,
# stamped with the new digest and generation, and painted.
# 66 assertions = 3 fixture + 5 collider +
# 8 through + 3 clear + 2 sliver + 2 buried + 2 enclosed + 2 flush + 2 scope +
# 6 queue/supersession (+1: a queued newer evaluation revokes the running
# check's paint) + 2 pin + 6 busy/reclaim + 5 neighbour/undecidable
# + 4 layered stack (+1: the same budget failure with the stack as the SOLID
# and a small node inside it — undecided, never dropped; +1: a solid edge
# through a plate with both probes out of budget is kept as a crossing) + 3
# two-enclosing-blocks (+1: two OVERLAPPING nodes of one reference are two
# answers, which a reference-scoped question cannot give) + 3 thin plate
# (+1: the tetrahedron that only leaves the plate) + 1 per-node parity
# budget + 2 colliders behind the poses (the rebuild and its digests; the
# crossing at the new pose) + 3 probe limit (the fixture straddles the
# diameter; the probed plate; the kept plate) + 2 rebuild under a check in
# flight (the superseded check; the rebuilding evaluation's stamped, painted
# answer).
# + 5 cast budget (the ray ceiling bounds CASTS, not the walk: a solid whose
# stray edges outnumber the whole budget still reports the unbounded
# answer untruncated; one ray short, the ceiling is stated with the count
# it left uncast).
# + 6 expected contacts (two bosses through the SAME board node: the control,
# a region round one of them leaving the other graded, the same region round
# the other with the two remainders adding up to the whole, both declared and
# the check passing, the falsifier — a contact 1.6 mm deep against a
# declaration allowing 0.5 — and a declaration that matched nothing).
# Also: a named part's collider is welded once and swapped back in for the
# legs that follow (builds vs generation), a verb arriving while a check
# runs QUEUES and reports the wait instead of bouncing, two verbs fired
# together both answer, and both bounds on that line still refuse.
test_interference.gd assertions=81

# Clearance between the evaluated solid and a reference: two bars crossing at
# right angles with 0.8 mm of air between them, the reference YAWED 30 degrees
# by its pose, where every vertex of either bar is more than 40 mm from the
# other, so the gap is face-to-face and a vertex-sampling check cannot find it.
# The exact distance runs in the worker (pinned by
# worker/tests/test_clearance.py); this suite pins everything the PANEL owns,
# against a stand-in backend that derives its answer from the blob the module
# actually wrote: the request naming geometry by hash and fitting the host's
# 64 KiB IPC cap, the upload-on-miss retry, content-addressed blob files that
# decode to the POSED world geometry, the sweep of blobs nothing references, an
# unchanged reference being named rather than re-sent, the answer's both-frame
# points and closest-first order, the mandatory tessellation tolerance and the
# status line quoting it, pass at 0.5 and a fail at 1.0 naming the node, node=
# scoping the question before it is asked, and four refusals (no required_mm, a
# node filter matching nothing, a worker error quoted verbatim, and a refused
# check reporting no pairs). Also the node a DISTANCE cannot see: a
# mesh-to-mesh distance is unsigned, so a node the latest interference report
# names comes back at 0 and fails while the node it does not name keeps its
# measured gap, the reply says whether the join happened, and a report about a
# different source is not joined. Also the channel cap itself: with a source
# long enough that only one target fits beside it, the request is SPLIT one
# target per message, every split message is under the limit and the answers
# merge back into one closest-first report; a source that leaves room for no
# target at all is refused with a reason instead of being handed to the host to
# refuse as payload_too_large. And the isolation two panels need: each module
# writes to its own blob directory, a clearance check leaves the interference
# check's own records exactly as it found them, and a panel releases its
# directory when it goes away.
# The cap is measured in UTF-8 BYTES, so a source of multibyte characters that
# fits by character count is refused rather than handed to the host over its
# byte limit. And the join carries DOUBT as well as overlap: a node the
# interference report lists as undecidable keeps its measured distance, says
# "containment undecidable: <reason>" and does not pass.
# The doubt travels in both directions: a report that could not decide whether
# the SOLID is inside a reference names no node, and doubts every node of that
# reference rather than being discarded.
# And a pin has to survive a re-pose: a call waiting for the worker's "never
# seen it" while the reference moves under it must still be able to upload the
# geometry it pinned, which it can only do while bodies are stored under their
# DIGEST rather than under the node that hashed to it.
# A cache file is only the file its NAME claims: a blob of the right length
# and the wrong bytes is rewritten rather than reused, or every retry hands
# the worker the same hash failure.
# The panel's records are live objects, so a re-pose rewrites a record's pose
# IN PLACE: a call whose pose is rewritten under it while it waits for the
# worker answers in the pose it was called with — local points converted
# through the copy it took, never the live record — and says the references
# moved. And a tolerance the worker could only GUESS (a curved face it cannot
# read) is not a bound: the check fails with a reason and a status line that
# says so. Accepting an unbounded tolerance requests an advisory grade only;
# both the overall and per-pair pass remain false. The
# stand-in grades like the worker (min_mm less the effective tolerance
# against required_mm), so a 0.505 mm gap under a 0.5 mm requirement with a
# 0.01 mm estimate fails in the worker's reply, and the opt-in regrades it on
# min_mm as advisory_pass with the reply saying the bar was waived.
# And the join is only as fresh as the poses and colliders it was measured
# at: a clean report about THIS source whose reference has since been moved
# (pose rewritten in place) or whose colliders have since been rebuilt is
# stale — nothing is joined, the check does not pass, and the reason says so —
# while a report stamped at the current state passes again. And NO report
# about this source is the same unknown: the DSL edited so the solid encloses
# a bar, asked before the new evaluation, does not pass ("interference
# evidence unavailable") while the unsigned distances are still reported.
# The vertices travel as float32: their quantization at the largest world
# coordinate is reported, stated in the bound and subtracted from bound_mm
# (2^-15 mm at the fixture's 300 mm), and a pose 1e8 mm out — 8 mm steps —
# is refused with the number rather than measured to a bar it cannot keep.
# 50 assertions = 3 fixture + 8 upload + 9 answer + 6 cap (+2: the multibyte
# fixture and the byte-measured refusal) + 4 refusal + 8 buried (+2: the
# undecidable node and the undecidable reference; +1: a stale report — moved
# poses or rebuilt colliders — is not a pass; +1: no report about this source
# is not a pass either) + 2 pin/blob across a re-pose (+1: the corrupted
# same-length file) + 1 pose rewritten in place + 2 unbounded tolerance (+1:
# the waiver grades on the distance alone, advisory only) + 2 part changes
# during await (mesh identity and local transform) + 2 quantization (the fixture's
# 2^-15 mm step reported and subtracted; the far pose refused) + 3 isolation.
# + 4 eviction (the fixture is bigger than the stand-in worker's cache; the
# first call in a session, which always passed; the SECOND call, which is
# where a panel that assumes residency across calls fails; and the retry
# carrying a path for every target rather than only the reported misses).
# Plus 9 ticket assertions: a measurement that outruns the verb's budget
# comes back running with a ticket and nothing measured, the ticket
# collects the SAME report the inline path produced, a spent ticket and an
# unknown one are refusals by name, a job still RUNNING long past the keep
# window is not swept and its late report is still collectable, and a
# finished report nobody collected does age out. Plus 2 flush-contact
# assertions: a pair at 0 mm whose interference join found no overlap is
# touching, not interference; lifted 1e-5 mm it is a positive distance with
# neither flag.
# Plus 6 expected-contact assertions: a designed 0.2 mm contact declared
# intended passes a 1 mm requirement; the same declaration over a pair 0.5 mm
# INTO the solid still reports interference and fails; a press fit declared a
# millimetre deep does cover that 0.5; a region excuses only the pair measured
# inside it and leaves the other pair of the same reference graded; a region
# holding no measured contact is unmatched; a declaration naming no reference
# is refused rather than dropped.
# Plus 3 lean-reply assertions: failing_only keeps the pair that misses its
# bar and drops the one that clears it even though an unbounded tessellation
# tolerance grades EVERY row false; the reply states how many pairs were
# hidden and states none when nothing was filtered; limit applies to what
# survives the filter, so the surviving row can be the further of the two —
# and LEAN IS THE DEFAULT: a caller passing neither flag still gets only the
# row that missed, with detail="full" the way back to every row.
# Plus 2 region assertions: four regions over the four contacts of ONE node
# all match, because a region is matched against every crossing the joined
# interference report named for the pair and not only its minimum-distance
# witness, while a fifth region over empty air is still reported unmatched;
# and the pair is still GRADED once, against the first declaration it
# answered to.
# Also: a part-scoped measurement joins the interference report for ITS OWN
# binding — not the document's, whose solid is the union — and refuses to
# pass when that part has no report, or when the walk that made it spent its
# ray budget, rather than falling back or certifying what nobody examined.
test_clearance.gd assertions=83

