# no two corners lined up) driven through minerva_cad_check_clearance with
# against=, with reference="all-pairs" and through
# minerva_cad_check_interference: the request sends each node once and names
# the pair by index, the stand-in worker derives 0.5 from the BYTES the panel
# wrote, the realising point comes back in the second reference's own frame,
# no tessellation tolerance is quoted for a measurement that tessellated
# nothing, and two parts that only miss each other list no interference at
# all. Plus the refusals: against= naming nothing mounted, and a reference
# measured against itself. And the z profile, on a KY-023 stand-in (a 16 x 16
# x 10 housing with a 2 x 2 stick to 42, posed off the origin): the housing
# footprint answers 10.1 where the stick's answers 42.1 — the falsifier a
# node-box reading cannot produce — a footprint wholly inside the top face
# with no triangle vertex in it is still measured, per_node lists both nodes
