# asserts the shaped reply still carries the answer — leanness that dropped
# the answer would pass a byte assertion on its own.
# 41 assertions = 4 addressing (two panels load; each registers its own host
# under its own title; each host answers with its own panel; the dispatcher
# answers a verb addressed by the tab title) + 5 the records digest (the
# fixture's digest really is thousands of characters; the reply fits 2 KB;
# what it carries is 16 hex; that hash still tells two reference sets apart;
# and the panel still holds the whole digest for the clearance join) + 5
# last_eval (a 12-node crossing report is kilobytes; the wire form fits the
# doc_write budget; the status line still names the nodes and the counts; the
# points are not in it and it says where they are; a clean reference is
# dropped and a failed one is kept) + 6 references (the full 45-node listing
# is kilobytes; the default fits its budget; it still names status, world box
# and node count; doubling the nodes does not grow it; detail="full" carries
# the pose, both frames and every node box; a reference= naming nothing is an
# error) + 5 clearance (50 pairs really are kilobytes; limit=5 fits its
# budget; it keeps the five CLOSEST; the verdict and the totals are
# unchanged; failing_only keeps only failures) + 2 obstructions (120
# crossings of two nodes collapse to two rows; each counts its rays, keeps
# the nearest crossing and states the axial range) + 2 the hole index (only
# addressable holes are indexed; the numbering is the pairing's own, with
# centres) + 3 the DSL census (slugs at the measured world centres with the
# clearance asked for; a skewed hole is named rather than guessed at; posts
# add at the same centres) + 2 await_eval (it returns the status the panel
# painted with the time it waited; a timeout reports the current status and
# cancels nothing) + 7 the edge listing (a panel and its host; a 700-edge
# registry sampled for drawing really is over a hundred kilobytes; the host
# copy the MCP listing verbs read carries none of those points, costs a fifth
# of the registry at most, and still names each edge's id, kind and both ends;
# the caller's own array still has the points, because that is what the panes
